{"id":"rs_tmp_aa52uw7mfnk","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"I realize the vault id is local to omp-ui's registry and omp wouldn't understand a .omp/config.yml key referencing it—plus committing a machine-local id to git seems wrong even though .omp is often gitignored. I'm recalling precedent from ADR-0047 (#738) where reviewRoster moved to ProjectRecord, and ADR-0005 which removed ProjectRecord.advisor.

The split appears to be: omp-owned settings go to config.yml, omp-ui-owned settings go to ProjectRecord, so I'll place this in ProjectRecord. The tradeoff is the same accepted loss as #738—it won't be git-shared, hand-editable, or visible to headless runs—but since the vault id is machine-specific, sharing it would actually be harmful anyway. Worth a quick check of ProjectRecord's current shape to confirm field placement.

