{"id":"rs_tmp_one3hknbsgd","type":"reasoning","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"I'm thinking about whether the vault registry id belongs in .omp/config.yml — it's really local and machine-specific to omp-ui's own registry, so omp itself wouldn't understand that key, and most of .omp is gitignored anyway per ADR-0018 with worktrees being linked separately. I recall a precedent in ADR-0047 where a similar local-only value was moved out of the shared config.

So ProjectRecord seems like the right place: the cost is that it's not git-shared and a headless omp running outside the app won't see it, but since the vault write tool is an omp-ui host tool, that's fine since only the app itself needs it. I should briefly cite the relevant field style from lines 109-155, and note as an unverified inference that omp's config validation might reject unknown keys, without asserting it as fact.

"}],"summary":[],"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ","format":"anthropic-claude-v1"}

